# Raw Data Documentation

This folder contains the source datasets used for the Sales Analysis Power BI project.

---

## Datasets Overview

* **Customers.xlsx**: Contains customer demographics and account details (19,119 records).
* **Products.xlsx**: Contains product catalog, pricing, cost, and categories (295 records).
* **Regions.xlsx**: Maps territory IDs to country codes and regional groups (10 records).
* **Sales.xlsx**: Transactional sales line items split across 4 yearly sheets: 2011, 2012, 2013, and 2014 (121,318 total records).

---

## Data Schema & Relationships

The dataset is structured as a **Star Schema**:

```text
       ┌───────────────┐
       │   Customers   │
       └───────┬───────┘
               │ (1:N)
               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐         ┌───────────────┐
│         Sales (Fact)        │◄──(N:1)─┤   Products    │
└──────────────┬──────────────┘         └───────────────┘
               │ (N:1)
               ▼
       ┌───────────────┐
       │    Regions    │
       └───────────────┘
Data Dictionary
1. Customers.xlsx (Sheet1)
CustomerID: Primary key for unique customer identifier.

StoreID: Store identifier code.

AccountNumber: Unique customer account number.

FirstName: Customer first name.

LastName: Customer last name.

Title: Customer title or honorific.

2. Products.xlsx (Sheet2)
ProductID: Primary key for unique product identifier.

ProductName: Full name and description of product.

ProductCategoryID: Numeric ID for main category.

Product Category: Main category (Bikes, Components, Clothing, Accessories).

Product Subcategory: Detailed product subcategory name.

ProductSubcategoryID: Numeric ID for subcategory.

Color: Product color variant.

StandardCost: Manufacturing or unit acquisition cost.

ListPrice: Retail catalog listing price.

SellStartDate: Date product became active in catalog.

SellEndDate: Date product was discontinued.

3. Regions.xlsx (Sheet1)
TerritoryID: Primary key for unique territory identifier.

Region Name: Name of territory or geographic region.

CountryRegionCode: ISO 2-letter country code (US, GB, DE, FR, AU).

Region Group: Major regional group (North America, Europe, Pacific).

4. Sales.xlsx (Sheets: 2011, 2012, 2013, 2014)
OrderDate: Date transaction took place.

CustomerID: Foreign key referencing Customers table.

TerritoryID: Foreign key referencing Regions table.

SalesOrderID: Sales order header identifier.

CarrierTrackingNumber: Shipment carrier tracking ID.

OrderQty: Number of units purchased.

ProductID: Foreign key referencing Products table.

SpecialOfferID: Applied promotion code.

UnitPriceDiscount: Discount amount applied per unit.

ModifiedDate: Date record was last updated.

ETL Requirements
Append/Union all 4 sheets in Sales.xlsx into a single consolidated Fact table.

Establish 1-to-Many single-direction relationships from Dimension tables to the Fact table.

Clean missing values in CarrierTrackingNumber and SellEndDate as needed.
